nale":"Defense and aerospace manufacturers routinely seek export licenses for controlled military and dual-use items, making licensing timelines a direct operational concern."},{"industry":"manufacturing","confidence":0.7,"rationale":"Manufacturers of industrial equipment and dual-use goods often require export licenses, so streamlined processing would reduce regulatory delays and costs."}],"plainSummary":"This bill requires the Bureau of Industry and Security to decide on export license applications within 90 days and to explain any delays beyond 120 days. It mandates quarterly reports to Congress on license processing and directs the Government Accountability Office to audit the bureau's review process. The measure aims to speed up and add transparency to the approval process for exporting controlled items.","classificationMethod":"llm","plain":{"whoItTouches":"Anyone who buys imported goods, and people who make goods here.","confidence":"crs-summary"},"topOverlap":{"bioguideId":"M001137","score":0.028535634956880454},"overlapCount":4},"meaning":{"percentile":77.69364253036757,"median":0.01073720309570498,"n":6339,"ordinary":[{"kind":"state-industry","text":"Technology is also the top donor sector for 4 other members from CA. That points to the industry being big in the state, not to anything about this member."}],"unattributedShare":0.7184999906751617}},{"billId":"119-hjres-78","bioguideId":"I000056","cycle":2026,"score":0.008623489520726614,"matches":[{"industry":"real-estate","donorAmount":43800,"donorShare":0.03349142432581705,"billConfidence":0.5,"contribution":0.006202115615892048},{"industry":"utilities-electric","donorAmount":11000,"donorShare":0.008411088301004283,"billConfidence":0.7,"contribution":0.002180652522482592},{"industry":"agriculture","donorAmount":1000,"donorShare":0.0007646443910003894,"billConfidence":0.85,"contribution":0.00024072138235197444}],"method":{"formula":"score = Σ_industries ( donorShare(industry) × billWeight(industry) ), where billWeight = classifierConfidence / Σ classifierConfidence. Range 0–1, read as a weighted share of disclosed itemized money.","donorProfileCycle":2026,"billClassificationMethod":"llm","unclassifiedDonorShare":0.7184999906751617},"bill":{"id":"119-hjres-78","congress":119,"billType":"hjres","billNumber":"78","title":"Providing for congressional disapproval under chapter 8 of title 5, United States Code, of the rule submitted by the United States Fish and Wildlife Service relating to \"Endangered and Threatened Wildlife and Plants; Endangered Species Status for the San Francisco Bay-Delta Distinct Population Segment of the Longfin Smelt\".","introducedDate":"2025-03-21","latestActionDate":"2025-05-05","latestActionText":"Received in the Senate.","policyArea":"Animals","subjects":["Administrative law and regulatory procedures","California","Congressional oversight","Department of the Interior","Endangered and threatened species","Fishes"],"sponsorBioguideId":"L000578","cosponsorCount":8,"committeeNames":[],"congressDotGovUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-joint-resolution/78","industries":[{"industry":"agriculture","confidence":0.85,"rationale":"Endangered species protections in the Bay-Delta region directly affect water allocation for agricultural irrigation in California's Central Valley."},{"industry":"utilities-electric","confidence":0.7,"rationale":"Water management and hydroelectric operations in the Bay-Delta system face regulatory constraints when species are listed as endangered."},{"industry":"waste-water","confidence":0.65,"rationale":"Water utilities and water districts must comply with endangered species protections that affect pumping, diversion, and discharge operations in the Bay-Delta."},{"industry":"real-estate","confidence":0.5,"rationale":"Development projects near Bay-Delta waterways face additional permitting requirements and habitat mitigation when endangered species are present."}],"plainSummary":"This resolution would overturn a federal rule that listed a specific population of longfin smelt fish in the San Francisco Bay-Delta region as endangered. If passed, the fish would lose protections under the Endangered Species Act that were granted in July 2024. The resolution uses a congressional review process that allows lawmakers to nullify recently issued federal regulations.","classificationMethod":"llm","plain":{"whoItTouches":"People who keep animals, and people who work with them.","confidence":"crs-summary"},"topOverlap":{"bioguideId":"F000480","score":0.02993303042113592},"overlapCount":8},"meaning":{"percentile":41.28411421359836,"median":0.01073720309570498,"n":6339,"ordinary":[],"unattributedShare":0.7184999906751617}}],"votes":[{"id":"a64a90b759595d68f3a8d502","billId":"119-hr-7008","date":"2026-07-22T16:51:00-04:00","question":"Yea-and-Nay","result":"Passed","position":"Yea","sourceUrl":"https://clerk.house.gov/evs/2026/roll280.xml"},{"id":"2afa499bcaceefdcecfa862a","billId":"119-hr-8800","date":"2026-07-22T16:37:00-04:00","question":"Yea-and-Nay","result":"Passed","position":"Yea","sourceUrl":"https://clerk.house.gov/evs/2026/roll278.xml"},{"id":"e69a4fe10a0cc4e4d35ffc3d","billId":"119-hr-6955","date":"2026-07-21T22:05:00-04:00","question":"Yea-and-Nay","result":"Passed","position":"Yea","sourceUrl":"https://clerk.house.gov/evs/2026/roll271.xml"},{"id":"c68077c5b6dd6fe8eb42bf43","billId":"119-hres-1438","date":"2026-07-21T14:39:00-04:00","question":"Recorded Vote","result":"Passed","position":"Aye","sourceUrl":"https://clerk.house.gov/evs/2026/roll254.xml"},{"id":"3944446cfd7ceaa28fbc0515","billId":"119-hres-1438","date":"2026-07-21T14:11:00-04:00","question":"Yea-and-Nay","result":"Passed","position":"Yea","sourceUrl":"https://clerk.house.gov/evs/2026/roll253.xml"},{"id":"7d8b32832c29b7b8b63de5d9","billId":"119-hr-1118","date":"2026-07-21T14:03:00-04:00","question":"2/3 Yea-And-Nay","result":"Passed","position":"Yea","sourceUrl":"https://clerk.house.gov/evs/2026/roll252.xm